# 5. For the later tasks of the track (nr-office-design-templates, -composition, -docx, -xlsx and the engine):
#    - `library::store::TemplateIndexer<L>` is the seam to `indexOfficeTemplates` (design-template-index.mjs, the templates task):
#      fn index(&self, lane: &InLane<L>, env: &Environment, data_dir: &Path, config: &LibraryConfig) -> Result<Value, String>.
#      The templates task implements it (answering the index object with `changed` and `count`, after writing template-index.json
#      with `library::write_json_atomic` when `changed || !previous.revision`) and the caller builds
#      `library::Context { lane, env, fetch: &HttpsFetch, indexer: &that }`. Do not write a second reader of the index or state file:
#      `library::read_template_index(proof, &paths)` and `library::write_state(lane, &paths, &state)` are design-template-index.mjs's
#      readTemplateIndex / writeState. The templates task also needs from here: `library::{library_paths, load_config, read_json,
#      write_json_atomic, canonical_path, sha256_file, safe_id, normalize_layouts, normalize_local_samples, MAX_LOCAL_TEMPLATE_COUNT,
#      MAX_SCAN_DEPTH, TEMPLATE_INSPECTOR_VERSION, TEMPLATE_FORMATS, template_format}`.
#    - The packaged templates: `Environment::process()` reads them from `<folder of the executable>/assets/templates`. The packaging
#      (prepare-runtime / electron-builder) places there native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/assets/templates/
#      mixdog-executive.pptx.mixdog.json (this task), mixdog-executive.pptx and mixdog-executive.mixdog-edit.pptx (nr-office-design-templates).
#      An archive-unpacked sidecar (physicalAsarPath) is not needed in the native build.
#    - The composition callers use: `library::resolve_office_design_library(&cx, &ResolveRequest {..})` -> the library object
#      `tokens::resolve_office_design(.., library: Option<&Value>, ..)` takes; `library::persist_office_design_binding`,
#      `library::record_office_composition_history` (CompositionRecord) and `library::read_office_composition_history`
#      (the context's `recent_compositions`).
#    - Not carried over: the AbortSignal of `syncOfficeDesignLibrary` / `resolveOfficeDesignLibrary` (the Rust calls run to their
#      own timeouts: 10 s to the manifest's response headers, 30 s per template).
